  "assumptions": {
    "allocation": "Judgment, not an audited marginal budget. Direct branch cost excludes central10% overhead; all60% nonbranch dollars retain cost.",
    "cessation": "Extra six-month quits among all offers beyond actual usual care; initial state difference(-1 smoker,+1 former smoker). Both later face background quitting, relapse and absorbing death. Smoking/quit hazards and utilities are independent priors, not trial conditional coefficients.",
    "recovery": "Two calendar years after initial six-month quit state have equal smoking/former mortality; then a lower former mortality applies. This is a coarse cohort-calendar recovery proxy, not exact time-since-each-quit/restart biology. No inherited Txt2stop lifetime coefficient.",
    "asthma": "All-age offers retain cost; central60% child share receives transferred trial benefit. One finite benefit year maximum, no death or caregiver credit. Child recipients disjoint from adult cessation; adult asthma health excluded.",
    "counterfactual": "Public APS, remediation, Kick It California, insured treatment, other charities and current funds remain baseline. Funding replacement is separate from incremental clinical effect and background later quitting.",
    "resources": "Gross gift+outside real inputs for all nominal offers. Outside$100 cessation medicine/clinician and$300 asthma supplies/provider effort are unpriced priors excluding branch cash/central overhead. Not net induced resources, transfers or downstream savings.",
    "geography": "US total modeled health; Bay means nine-county Bay Area, not all18 counties. Central cessationBay/SF75%/5%;asthma80%/8%, independent unverified future-residence shares. Non-US unquantified.",
    "harms": "Shared per-added-offer and independent QALY losses are gift-date PV, excluding worsening in state/symptom differences. All age asthma offers can incur shared harms even when child benefit excluded.",
    "scale": "Only illustrative$100k local margin; bounded computational inputs do not verify linear expansion."
  }
